  "change_summary": "Fixed feedforward (K=0.885, uff~0.51) under-drives the weakened heater by ~0.25. Added online DC-gain estimator Kest with bumpless transfer to feedforward plus stronger conditional integral (Ki 0.014->0.032, limits -0.40/+0.55). Kest starts at nominal 0.885 and only adapts near steady state (|dy|<0.0012, |u-u_avg|<0.07, |y-y_avg|<0.03, elapsed>90s), learning K_raw=(y_avg-0.05)/u_avg with Tc~90s. Nominal plant stays at K~0.88-1.0, degraded converges to ~0.58, raising uff from 0.51 to ~0.77 so integral does not have to wind up for 400s.",
  "design_rationale": "Cooling at u=0 unchanged (E5 tau~151s vs E3 152s, same immediate fall, same ambient ~0.05-0.10) rules out outflow/sensor/delay. Heating slopes 35-60% low (E6 0.104->0.33 in 240s vs E1 0.051->0.395 in 180s; E7 slope ~0.0010 vs expected ~0.0027) and y_ss(0.75)~0.491 equals old y_ss(0.5) imply b and K scaled by ~0.62-0.68 with same a=1/tau. Fixed uff therefore leaves ~0.04-0.15 steady error, matching monitoring MAE 0.0038->0.031. Ratio estimator directly identifies new K when settled; gating on derivative and stability prevents learning during initial ramp. Bumpless transfer (integ-=delta_uff) keeps u continuous so nominal transient unchanged. Stronger but anti-windup integral covers residual during adaptation. Clamps Kest to [0.42,1.15] and safety derate >0.80 preserved for both plants.",
